Entitlement to Hospital Insurance (HI) under Environmental Health Hazards (EHH) Medicare can exist concurrently with HI entitlement based on age, disability, or ESRD. It is advantageous for a beneficiary entitled to HI based on age, disability, or ESRD to file an application for EHH Medicare if any one of the following applies:

• The beneficiary is not currently enrolled in Supplementary Medical Insurance (SMI);

• The beneficiary is paying a SMI premium surcharge because of late enrollment;

• The date of entitlement to EHH Medicare would be earlier than the date of entitlement to Medicare based on other criteria; or

• The beneficiary, who is enrolled in Premium HI, Premium HI and SMI, or SMI only, can now receive free HI.

NOTE: A beneficiary who already has Medicare based on age, disability, or ESRD may choose to apply for EHH Medicare to have the beneficiary's record reflect entitlement to Medicare based on EHH.

If you cannot obtain primary evidence, consider obtaining statements from two reliable, disinterested individuals who have firsthand knowledge of the claimant’s presence in Lincoln County, Montana. Solicit these statements only after you exhaust all attempts to secure evidence. The individuals may include, but are not limited to, the following:

